  "id": "Compound::DB00482 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "Celecoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, exhibits a strong binding interaction with multiple Ca5, Ca6, and Ca5b proteins, all of which are involved in carbonate dehydratase activity. This suggests that Celecoxib may modulate a shared biochemical pathway in cells expressing these proteins. The observed involvement of Ca9 in the carbonic anhydrase activity indicates that Celecoxib could potentially influence cellular processes associated with Ca9, possibly through the inhibition of carbonate dehydratase. The consistent evidence across three paths, with similar scores, supports a mechanistic link between Celecoxib and Ca9, particularly through the modulation of carbonate dehydratase activity. The integration of these findings suggests that Celecoxib may exert its effects on Ca9 via a common pathway involving carbonate dehydratase, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional relevance.",
